WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.610
Class 3-B?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.760
Ms. Kuroi!

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.920
Yeah, yeah...

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:35.420
Hey...

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.380
What are we in line for?

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.800
Do you know, Yuki-chan?

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:39.550
No idea...

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.430
Now, now...

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.010
There you have it.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:44.470
Too bad.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.980
I also got a miss.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.390
Um...

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.430
I drew a winner.

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:50.180
Me too!

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:53.600
My true friends!

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.520
What about me?

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.030
<i>I'm gonna follow you through.</i>

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.900
<i>No matter the pain.</i>

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.070
<i>Through the darkeness of this world if I must.</i>

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:04.320
Big guy blocking...
<i>Through the darkeness of this world if I must.</i>

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.700
<i>'Cause you'll be there to shine the way.</i>
Big guy blocking...

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.450
<i>'Cause you'll be there to shine the way.</i>

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.460
Here.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.080
<i>Past the end of the future.</i>

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.670
<i>Won't let weakness...</i>

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.220
<i>...break down my soul.</i>

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.000
That was incredible.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.460
I was quite moved.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:22.810
The first person who came out was so cool.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.060
That guy?

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:24.970
No?

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.510
People actually go for that, huh?

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:30.610
Konata, you haven't said a word.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.940
The whole fatigue setting in after an event's over thing, huh?

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.620
I guess I was a bit moved myself.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.070
I wonder what this feeling is...

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.220
What are you doing?

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.880
Come on. We're going now.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.000
You're really proactive about some odd things.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.340
Because today's our last chance to
see the cherry blossoms in full bloom.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.720
When you put something off to tomorrow...

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.180
...or the day after...

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.220
...it ends up raining...

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.390
...or the petals start falling.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.270
Oh, yeah.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:14.490
What happened to the goldfish from the summer festival?

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.270
Actually...

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:18.440
...I ended up feeding it too much...

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.150
...and it ended up like this.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:19.820
Huge!

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.820
Shogun?!

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.780
I took a little too good care of it.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.490
Wait a minute.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.950
Are you sure you didn't feed it something funny?

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.700
That's no longer a goldfish!

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:32.370
I can only pray that it's because he's living a good life.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.580
Are you going to eat it?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.620
How could I?!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:40.750
There's an anime where animals a guy took
good care of return as humans to serve him.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.130
You always bring up hardcore references.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.720
I should probably put it on a diet...

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.800
Kagami.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.150
Are you thinking about getting a replacement?

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.980
It's gotten pretty chilly.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.190
We should probably head home.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:02.320
When you wear daytime clothes to see
nighttime cherry blossoms, it gets cold.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.940
And your butt gets cold when you sit down.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.740
I've heard that the average temperature in March...

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.370
...is close to the average temperature in December...

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:13.410
...and April and November are quite similar.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:17.040
If it were November or December, I'd definitely wear a lot more.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.330
In March and April...

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:19.920
...you just tend to dress lighter.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.840
Isn't it because you're sick of wearing winter clothes?

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:27.570
Maybe it's a way of expressing
how you want it to be spring already.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.220
You look like you're fine, Kagami.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.020
Maybe it's because you're wearing...

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:33.780
Came prepared.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.220
I'm not wearing any!

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.740
<i>That's all you get today, Goldy.</i>

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.910
<i>It'd be a problem...</i>

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.540
<i>...if he showed up as a wife beater...</i>

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:52.280
<i>As if...</i>

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.200
<i>What's wrong with Sis?</i>
<i>As if...</i>

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.750
Man, that really smarts...

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:01.250
I have really delicate skin.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.960
This season is brutal for me.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.050
Sounds like a pain.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:07.090
And I stay in the house most of the time.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:10.180
They have a lot of goods that help for allergies.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.640
Why don't you buy some?

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.060
Transform!

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:24.900
I see!

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:25.780
This works!

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.820
Reduces the effect of allergies by 99%!

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:31.000
Now he's suspicious on the outside and the inside.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.960
Don't get in trouble with the police.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.870
I'm going to go do some shopping.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.250
Have fun!

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.160
Want to come along?

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.570
Nope!

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.330
Wait, Dad.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.080
You're going shopping like that?

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.000
Of course.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Or it'd defeat the purpose.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.460
Here's our next story.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:47.920
Last night around eleven...

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.050
...a woman broke into a convenience store...

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.800
...and attempted to steal the cash.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.220
Hey, Yu-chan.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.100
What is it?

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.600
Aren't there a lot more robbers
disguised with allergy gear this time of year?

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.350
It sounds possible.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.190
Freeze.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.190
How did this happen?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.110
Tomorrow?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:06.770
Sure.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.610
Haven't done that in a while.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:09.320
That's right.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.780
Plus, I'm already done with my homework.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.450
What did you just say?!

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:14.490
You finished your homework?!

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:15.240
For real?!

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:15.870
Unbelievable!

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:16.280
Sorry.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.110
I lied.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:20.500
Yeah, you know how you have to lie on April Fool's?

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.160
Good thing I remembered.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.750
No, seriously...

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.880
And you have no intention of doing it, huh?

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.210
You must be bored.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:31.220
You're the only person who would call at this hour just to lie.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.020
Anyway, see you tomorrow.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.140
Yes, this is Izumi.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.180
This is Kuroi.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.960
Is this the Izumi residence?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.280
Teacher.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:42.850
Izumi, it's me.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:43.390
Sorry.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.980
I accidentally overwrote a save file...

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.240
...on a game I borrowed from you.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.860
Just lying! Hey!

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.110
Fooled you!

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.200
Today's April Fool's!

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.660
<i>There was somebody else as bored as me...</i>

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.280
Teacher.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.040
What's up?

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.790
The other day, Miyuki-san said...

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:04.460
<i>Even someone like Ms. Kuroi can be a teacher...</i>

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.380
<i>...so getting a certificate must be a cakewalk.</i>

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:07.970
...something like that.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:10.050
That brat...

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:11.890
So the sweet talk was just an act...

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.590
Um, Teacher.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.010
I was joking...

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:18.180
Konata called me just so she could lie.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.400
Honestly...

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.690
Did you lie to anyone today?

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.560
That's unusual.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.030
What was it?

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.900
I-I just did.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.440
I lied about lying.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:32.780
Th-That's hard to get.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.360
And there's no need to force yourself to lie.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.580
Wh-What was Kona-chan's lie like?

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.450
Something about finishing her homework on her own.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:44.460
In retrospect, I really shouldn't have fallen for it.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:45.120
It's impossible.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.580
If she lied, then she hasn't done her homework yet, right?

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:49.840
Well, knowing her...

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.550
...she definitely hasn't done it!

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:52.720
I see...

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.050
You were just thinking...

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.640
...that it's a good thing you aren't alone, right?

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:58.560
No...

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:03.930
Konata.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.230
Do you have a minute?

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.200
Is that interesting?

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.040
Unique.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:17.660
I see.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:20.990
Konata.

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:24.250
I'm actually thinking about remarrying.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:27.330
Wait, I know that you're against it.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:30.170
In your mind, Kanata will always be your only moth—

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:32.420
What?

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.590
You're okay with it?

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:34.920
If I get remarried?

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.140
Why not?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.050
B-But...

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.090
You know...

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:40.930
She'll be your new mother?

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:43.360
What will my new mother be like?

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:45.930
Uh...

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:47.060
Well...

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:50.450
Wh-When you put it that way...

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:52.770
Okay. Here's the next question.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.980
What is the kenjogo form for iku (to go)?

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:56.690
It's gotta be ukagau (to inquire)!

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:58.040
Piece of cake!

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:59.070
That's right.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.600
It's to inquire.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.170
That should be the correct answer.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.330
Sounds right.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.000
The correct answer is mairu (to visit).

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.920
O-On second thought, that's right...

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.210
Yeah...

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.120
I went with the flow there.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.830
<i>What's with the weird atmosphere?</i>

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:14.960
Me too...

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.440
<i>This is what happens when
you're positive you're right.</i>

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.590
Multiple choice quiz, question one.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:23.890
Which prefecture does not border the ocean?

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:26.140
A. Ibaraki.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.930
B. Tochigi.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.270
C. Kyoto.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:30.690
It's B!

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:31.440
B, right?

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:33.160
This is easy.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.370
The correct answer is B!

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:36.820
Next question.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.900
Of the hardest known problems in mathematics...

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.990
...the theorem proven by...

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:47.540
...Princeton's Sir Wiles in 1994 was...

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.330
A. The Pythagorean theorem.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.500
B. Taylor's theorem.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.840
C. Fermat's last theorem.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.470
<i>Why is everyone so eager when the answer is obvious...</i>

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:03.180
<i>...but then they keep quiet when they're not sure?</i>

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:08.270
Since it's spring break, we should visit Miyuki-san's house.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.180
That sounds good.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.490
It's pretty far so I've never been there before.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:15.110
Miyuki-san's family is rich, right?

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:16.490
I wonder what it's like.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:18.730
A pool in her backyard?

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:19.690
Nah...

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:21.780
A security fence around the whole place.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.240
No, it's probably a lot more normal.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.620
She probably has a pet.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.910
A ferret might fit her image.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:29.200
A white one.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.960
Nah, gotta be a dog.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.250
A huge, white dog.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.250
With a huge yard and a white parasol.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:35.750
She might have a dog.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.010
That's how the conversation went.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.050
You're welcome to visit...

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:42.300
...but please don't expect too much.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.470
I'm sorry to say that I have no pets.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:48.640
However, while we don't have a white, big dog or a parasol...

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.320
...one of our neighbors does.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:56.160
And the neighbor's kid is entering Ryouou this year.

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:59.110
She's also been invited. Do you want to come?

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:01.530
My friend's cousin...

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.610
...is entering Ryouou.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.990
It's a small world after all.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.450
S-So sleepy...

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:12.580
Honestly...

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.970
It's because you got used to sleeping all morning.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:15.670
Konata.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:16.290
Yo.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.170
What?

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:19.590
You also got used to sleeping in?

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:22.340
I've been gaming for three days straight...

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:23.760
I'm about to die...

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.220
<i>The only thing they have in common is their laziness!</i>

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.720
We're in the same class again!

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:30.510
You're right!

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:31.560
That's great.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:32.770
Good morning.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.390
Good morning, Yuki-chan.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:35.230
Good morning.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.630
You're in our class.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.730
Indeed.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:39.900
That's wonderful.

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.860
Let's have another great year!

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:43.110
Let's!

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.830
We're in the same class!

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.830
I-I hope we have a wonderful year!

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:52.840
So do I.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.590
Kagami's the only one in a different class again.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:04.300
I see you guys all the time anyway.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:07.170
If we weren't in different classes, you'd wear me out.

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:07.370
That's too bad...
If we weren't in different classes, you'd wear me out.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.510
Sis...
That's too bad...

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:08.620
No big deal.
Sis...
That's too bad...

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.430
No big deal.

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:10.970
It's the same as usual.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:12.720
Besides, someone like Konata...

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:15.100
...will come borrowing notes or textbooks.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.600
You know me well.

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:18.220
So that's that...

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:19.400
Go on ahead.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.030
See you later!

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.610
Yo, Hiiragi!

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:28.110
What class you in?

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.640
We're in the same class again!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.010
If you count middle school...

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.160
...that makes five years straight?

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.700
Let's have another good year.

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:37.710
Huh?

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:42.670
Some heartless people only look for their top priorities.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:43.630
There, there.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:46.360
We're like part of the background!

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:51.180
I wonder how class assignments are decided.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.390
They might try to avoid grouping all the good students together...

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:56.930
...or try to divide up relatives...

00:12:56.930 --> 00:13:00.690
...or split up the troublemakers as much as possible.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:02.440
At least that's what I've heard.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:05.070
It probably depends on the school.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:09.660
In TV shows, all the troublemakers end up in one class.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.200
It's more exciting that way.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.580
But high schools are supposed to gather people of the same level...

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.370
...so there shouldn't be any big troublemakers.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.290
That's true.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:18.870
Miyuki...

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:22.960
That's where you say, "You need to
realize that you're a troublemaker."

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.040
You don't want to be put on the same level as her, right?

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:25.430
No, that's not true...
You don't want to be put on the same level as her, right?

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:26.670
No, that's not true...

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.260
The bell already rang.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.550
Teacher sure is late.

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.230
That's right.

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:35.850
Everybody, sit down!

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:36.430
<i>Still good.</i>

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:37.390
<i>Barely made it.</i>

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:38.560
<i>No good.</i>

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:42.000
I'm your homeroom teacher, Kuroi.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.610
Y'all advanced a year in school now...

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:45.400
...so stop acting like you're on vacation...

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.230
...and start working hard.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.410
<i>Th-That wasn't convincing at all!</i>

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:54.530
Well, I won't bug you about studying all the time...

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.120
...but this is your last year in high school...

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.750
...so I want you to have a meaningful experience.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:58.540
Okay.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.120
Let's get straight to class duties.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.120
Takara.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:03.290
Can you be class representative for the first semester?

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:03.960
Yes.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:09.010
Once you've been class rep, it gets attached to your image.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.470
That's true.

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:12.470
Though I don't have any problem with it.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.680
The teacher usually decides roles for the first semester.

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:17.390
Because of all the unfamiliar faces...

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.560
...it's hard for the students to choose.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:24.270
In Ms. Kuroi's case, isn't it less
work for her if she chooses Miyuki-san?

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:25.730
I can hear you.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:29.070
Teacher's hair was all wild.

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:32.740
But it looks like we'll have another fun class with Ms. Kuroi.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.990
Well, she's a fun person.

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:38.700
The class atmosphere usually depends on the teacher...

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:39.450
I see.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:40.290
I get it.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:44.790
So you two are blaming your laziness on your teacher.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:46.340
I can hear you.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:47.670
I'm Iwasaki.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:48.710
Nice to meet you.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.880
That girl's pretty cute.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.800
I was in the same middle school as her.

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:53.930
She never talks.

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:54.720
And she's a downer.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:57.100
And all she does is read. It's creepy.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:00.230
<i>But she's actually a really nice person.</i>

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.520
<i>So I'm the only one who knows.</i>

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:03.520
<i>I feel a little special.</i>

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.780
Next.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:05.690
Y-Yes!

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:08.570
<i>The first impression is important.</i>

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.490
<i>I have to be cheerful.</i>

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:12.740
I'm Yutaka Kobayakawa.

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:13.860
Though I may look this way...

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:16.620
...I didn't skip here from grade school.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:17.370
Just kidding.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:18.950
Skipped?

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:19.030
What was that?

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:20.200
<i>H-Huh?</i>

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.870
<i>Huh? What?</i>

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:25.580
<i>Did Big Sister's influence turn me into a maniac?</i>

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:26.920
In that case...

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:28.840
I'd like to decide on class duties...

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:31.510
Anybody interested in being class representative?

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:32.670
Guess not.

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:33.720
Iwasaki.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.380
You were class rep in middle school.

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:36.430
Go for it.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:37.550
Really?

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.140
Can you do it, Iwasaki?

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:40.260
I'm sorry.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.100
I'm planning on a different duty.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.850
I'd prefer someone with experience...

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:46.650
What are you planning on?

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.200
Working in the library?

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.080
The nurse's office.

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:53.820
Teacher!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:54.980
I'll be class representative!

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.530
<i>She's a really nice person!</i>

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:57.020
Cherry blossoms bloom into future, love, and dreams.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:58.120
Spring...

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:58.700
Cherry blossoms bloom into future, love, and dreams.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.950
...tends to gives you the feeling that...

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:01.410
I can't stop my heart from racing.
...tends to gives you the feeling that...

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.410
...something's about to begin.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:04.580
I can't stop my heart from racing.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:05.000
A new meeting.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.870
Let the two of us spend...

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:08.580
A new life.

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.160
...this touching season together.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.460
A new love.

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:13.840
This moment of a lifetime...

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:15.840
With your childhood friend...

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:16.380
The upperclassman you admired...
This moment of a lifetime...

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:17.930
This meeting is the beginning of our story.

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.720
Or a strange transfer student...?

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:22.720
A little anxiety and a lot of expectation...
Cherry blossom petals dance in the air...

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:24.140
It's what they call 5 seconds to falling in love.

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:24.350
...carrying our wishes...

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.480
Also known as MK5.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.190
That's the happy image you get...

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:31.400
But in reality, you have to start over with people you don't know...

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.650
...so it's depressing.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.400
I'm already used to it.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:35.780
You've got it easy.

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:36.950
Big Sister!

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.160
Yu-chan.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.540
Haven't seen you since morning.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:40.780
That's right.

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:42.260
Not since morning.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:43.160
Oh.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.080
This is the person I told you about...

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.010
The one who helped me.

00:16:47.010 --> 00:16:48.250
So you found her.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.000
Nice to meet you!

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:51.790
See?

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:53.710
Just like I said.

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:55.010
I knew she would pass.

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:55.760
Okay.

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:56.800
But Yu-chan...

00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:00.230
You forgot that she could have passed but chosen not to come.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.930
It worked out in the end so it's okay!

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:05.430
By the way, what are you doing?

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:07.770
We wanted to check where the nurse's office is.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.270
Since I'll probably be visiting it.

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:10.820
I see.

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:12.560
Show us the way, Big Sister.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:13.440
Okay.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.440
Leave it to your big sister.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:23.000
Where is the nurse's office?

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:26.280
I've never gone before so I don't know.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.330
Hey now.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:30.540
You've been here two years, and you
don't know where the nurse's office is?

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:33.590
Well, doesn't that just mean I had a healthy two years?

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:35.880
No, you went there for your physicals.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:36.630
Oh, yeah.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.920
I don't think I've ever been to the art room.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:41.970
If you choose music for your fine
art, you won't have a chance to go.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:45.890
I myself have never stepped foot in the judo hall.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:49.480
I didn't even know we had a tea room until recently.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.480
Even after going to the same school for three years, huh?

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:56.570
I guess everybody only goes to the places they need to.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.490
I rarely go to the study room.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.990
I go there!

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.240
Unexpected.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:04.700
The silence...

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:06.990
It's perfect for sleeping.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:07.740
Really...

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:09.290
Oh...

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:13.420
Yu-chan went to find the nurse's office
with the girl who helped her during exams.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.500
They ended up in the same class.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:16.710
It's a miracle.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:18.260
When you stop and think about it...

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:21.970
...the fact that I met and became friends
with Kona-chan and Yuki-chan at this school...

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:23.010
...might be a miracle!

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:24.890
Pretty much.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:29.850
We can only be here together for one more year.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.770
But Kagami was the only one in a different class the whole time.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.320
Don't mention that.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:41.650
The correct answer is B. hemlock.

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:44.250
It'll be on the test so keep that in mind.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:45.620
Hey.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:46.620
Wake up, Izumi!

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:47.740
Potemkin!

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:49.370
What were you dreaming about?

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:50.870
Sorry.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:55.010
I'm actually concentrating really hard on not falling asleep.

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:56.540
But Teacher...

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:57.960
They still come!

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.500
Those demons of sleep...

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.460
With no warning!

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.550
No way to defend!

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.440
A full-out attack!

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:06.470
Not sure why you're trying to explain yourself...

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.930
Maybe this will help you stay awake.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:11.640
Miyuki-san, you don't fall asleep in class, right?

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:13.520
Is there some kind of trick?

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:15.730
I wouldn't call it a trick...

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:17.980
But I really need my sleep...

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.360
...so I go to bed at eleven.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:21.990
By the way...

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:23.980
...I went to bed at ten during our second year.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:24.700
<i>No good.</i>

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.990
<i>No chance.</i>

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.330
<i>Can't copy that!</i>

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:38.090
I remember that this stuff was important so I took notes...

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:41.090
...but I was asleep half the time so I have no idea what I wrote.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:42.710
I can't tell.

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:45.630
But just looking at this makes me feel good about myself.

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:48.600
This is proof that I tried to study.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:51.530
But what did I write down...

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.350
Aren't those formulas?

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:54.850
Ms. Kuroi.

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:55.560
Wow!

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:58.190
You can understand this abomination!

00:19:58.190 --> 00:19:58.980
Pretty much.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:03.490
But that means you weren't dreaming about world history.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:06.610
Okay.

00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:11.330
Big Sister, you're still up?

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.420
<i>Guess it stinks.</i>

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:14.700
<i>Oops.</i>

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.000
<i>It's already this late?</i>

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.960
<i>Maybe somebody's on.</i>

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:21.250
<i>You never learn, huh?</i>

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:22.960
<i>Can't wait for tomorrow.</i>

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:30.010
Good lucky!

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:34.180
This is Lucky Channel, broadcasting to the whole wide world!

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:36.980
I'm your navigator, Akira Pretty Kogami!

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:39.650
And I'm the assistant, Minoru Shiraishi.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.020
We've already reached the 15th episode of Lucky Channel.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:43.610
Huh?

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.150
This is the 15th episode?

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.320
Yes...

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.280
Then isn't this your last one?

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:50.230
Uh...

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:51.250
See ya.

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:53.240
Didn't you hear?

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:55.580
The producers told me that...

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.750
...starting with episode 16, the show
would feature Akira Kogami alone...

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.040
...so good luck.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:02.540
Uh, that's...

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:04.380
Hey!

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:05.550
Gotcha!

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:07.720
April Fool's!

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:09.800
Oh...

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:10.550
That's what it was...

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:11.340
That's right...
See ya, sucker.

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:13.560
Anyway, you were pretty pumped.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.060
During the Jam of Haruhi...

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:17.820
...the MC was someone who looked like you.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:19.480
Really?

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:20.440
Couldn't be...

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:23.270
So when am I going to get a concert?

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:25.610
No idea...

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.890
They better tell me early...

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:31.840
...since my schedule's filled up for the near future.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:32.950
I'll go check right away!

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:33.530
Hurry.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:34.230
Look!

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:34.490
Hurry.

00:21:34.490 --> 00:21:35.330
The East is...

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:35.790
Hurry it up...

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:36.910
...is burning red!

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:38.450
Hurry... it... up...

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:40.790
Circle.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:42.510
Producer says okay.

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:44.600
Next time?

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.000
Understood!

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.330
Next week during this time...

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:48.970
...we'll have a live concert featuring Akira Kogami!

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:51.430
N-Next week?!

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:52.640
F-F-For real?!

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:53.970
They secured a stage?

00:21:53.970 --> 00:21:54.600
Yes.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:55.810
He pulled some strings to get it done.

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:57.290
And bend.

00:21:57.510 --> 00:21:58.250
Awesome!

00:21:58.250 --> 00:21:59.000
Alright!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.600
Not bad, Itou!

00:22:00.600 --> 00:22:01.230
Man...

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:02.220
I can't wait to hear you sing.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:02.810
No way!

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:03.270
Seriously?

00:22:03.270 --> 00:22:03.930
For real?!

00:22:03.930 --> 00:22:04.770
Leave the MC duties to me.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:05.690
So you do know what you're doing.

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:06.400
Believe it or not I'm well-known for my abilities as an MC.

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.320
I'm going all out!

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:09.740
There you have it, everyone!

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:12.070
Let's go crazy next week!

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:13.450
Then we'll see you next week!

00:22:13.450 --> 00:22:14.950
Bye-bee!

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:15.580
Oh, yes.

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:18.040
Will Minoru Shiraishi really be back next week?

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.500
I'm a lieutenant.

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:21.420
Hey.

00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:22.990
What are you going to sing first?

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:24.260
You're not starting with Sunny Sunshiny, right?

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:28.660
The first song isn't Sunny Sunshiny, right?

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:29.960
Oh, he already started.

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:41.940
What are you singing first?

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:55.450
Anyway, in that case...

00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:57.490
Whenever you're ready.

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:07.200
Whenever you're ready.

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:33.000
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:33.940
I'm Inori.

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:34.720
I'm Matsuri.

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:35.530
I'm Miki.

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:36.510
I'm Tadao.

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:37.130
Next time:

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:37.970
Ring.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:39.930
Look forward to next time!
